# Liste_Pearl — env template (Expo managed workflow)
# Copy to .env for `npx expo start`. Expo reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OTP v2 — Firebase Phone Auth (Web SDK — Expo compatible)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy values from Firebase console → Project Settings → General →
# Liste app (Android OR iOS — same apiKey works for both via SDK).
# Leave blank → useOtpSender returns shouldFallback=true → legacy
# /users/verify-otp/ flow keeps working.
#
# NOTE: the Firebase Web SDK needs a reCAPTCHA widget. Expo archived
# expo-firebase-recaptcha. Until a replacement is wired, the Firebase
# path in useOtpSender falls back to legacy by design (twilio and
# whatsapp providers still work server-side). See services/otpauth/README.md.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIza...
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=pearl-streets-c3b29.firebaseapp.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=pearl-streets-c3b29
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:413430640595:android:...

# Staging backend (already configured in services/config.js by default)
# API_URL=https://pythonapi.digiexports.in/api/v1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe — publishable key (LIVE or TEST mode)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aligned with secret key on backend. Use pk_test_... for dev, pk_live_... for prod.
# NEVER commit .env — only .env.example. Rotate the key in Stripe dashboard if leaked.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxx
